{
  "story_id": "town_npc_5",
  "name": "Nadia",
  "first_greeting": "New in town? Try not to break anything.",
  "repeat_greeting": "Hello. Need something?",
  "trusted_greeting": "Good to see you. I've got a question for you later.",
  "cooldown_greeting": "I'm busy. Come back in a bit.",
  "redirect": "Right. What's next?",
  "subject_change": "Another problem, if you please.",
  "nodes": {
    "root": {
      "speech": "Do you need something fixed, or are we just talking?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I've got a building problem.",
          "to": "build"
        },
        {
          "text": "What do you think of redstone?",
          "to": "redstone"
        },
        {
          "text": "Got any puzzles for me?",
          "to": "puzzles"
        },
        {
          "text": "Would you plan a trip with me?",
          "to": "planning"
        },
        {
          "text": "How's everything going here?",
          "to": "town"
        }
      ]
    },
    "build": {
      "speech": "Describe the problem. Properly, please.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I want a door that opens automatically.",
          "to": "door"
        },
        {
          "text": "Something's broken, but I don't know why.",
          "to": "broken"
        },
        {
          "text": "I haven't actually started building.",
          "to": "no_plan"
        }
      ]
    },
    "door": {
      "speech": "Pressure plates? Redstone? What kind of automatic door do you mean?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Just a simple pressure plate.",
          "to": "door_simple",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "I want something elaborate.",
          "to": "door_fancy"
        },
        {
          "text": "I hadn't thought that far.",
          "to": "no_plan"
        }
      ]
    },
    "door_simple": {
      "speech": "Then start simple. A plate and a door. See if it works before adding more.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "That's sensible.",
          "to": "build_success",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "But I wanted something impressive.",
          "to": "door_fancy"
        }
      ]
    },
    "door_fancy": {
      "speech": "Fine. Make sure you can still open it when the mechanism breaks.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I hadn't thought of failure cases.",
          "to": "build_success",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "It'll never break.",
          "to": "door_overconfident"
        }
      ]
    },
    "door_overconfident": {
      "speech": "Famous last words. Test it anyway.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Alright, I will.",
          "to": "build_success"
        },
        {
          "text": "You sound paranoid.",
          "to": "no_plan"
        }
      ]
    },
    "broken": {
      "speech": "Good. At least you're not pretending you know. What changed before it stopped?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I changed some redstone.",
          "to": "broken_redstone"
        },
        {
          "text": "I changed nothing I can remember.",
          "to": "broken_unknown"
        },
        {
          "text": "I hit it a few times.",
          "to": "broken_hit"
        }
      ]
    },
    "broken_redstone": {
      "speech": "Undo the last change, then test each part. One thing at a time.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I can try that.",
          "to": "build_success",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "Can't I replace the whole thing?",
          "to": "broken_replace"
        }
      ]
    },
    "broken_unknown": {
      "speech": "Then we begin by observing what it does, not what you hoped it would do.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Okay, I'll check it carefully.",
          "to": "build_success",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "That sounds slow.",
          "to": "no_plan"
        }
      ]
    },
    "broken_hit": {
      "speech": "Please tell me you're joking.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I was. Mostly.",
          "to": "build_success"
        },
        {
          "text": "No. Did I make it worse?",
          "to": "broken_unknown"
        }
      ]
    },
    "broken_replace": {
      "speech": "You can, but you might recreate the same fault. Find the cause first.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Fair point.",
          "to": "build_success",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "I'll take my chances.",
          "to": "no_plan"
        }
      ]
    },
    "no_plan": {
      "speech": "Right. Then you've found the problem before you've even built anything.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Can you help me plan it?",
          "to": "planning"
        },
        {
          "text": "I just like improvising.",
          "to": "improvise"
        }
      ]
    },
    "improvise": {
      "speech": "You can improvise. Just don't call it a mystery when it fails.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Fair.",
          "to": "planning"
        },
        {
          "text": "You're no fun.",
          "to": "town"
        }
      ]
    },
    "build_success": {
      "speech": "Test it in a small space before you trust it with your house.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I'll do that.",
          "to": "redstone",
          "effect": "warm"
        },
        {
          "text": "What other systems do you build?",
          "to": "redstone"
        }
      ]
    },
    "redstone": {
      "speech": "It's useful. It rewards patience and punishes bad wiring.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "What's the first thing to learn?",
          "to": "redstone_begin"
        },
        {
          "text": "I made a machine that keeps breaking.",
          "to": "broken"
        },
        {
          "text": "I prefer doing things by hand.",
          "to": "redstone_manual"
        }
      ]
    },
    "redstone_begin": {
      "speech": "A lever, some dust and a door. Learn what each part does before building a contraption.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I can start there.",
          "to": "build_success",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "That's too basic.",
          "to": "redstone_complex"
        }
      ]
    },
    "redstone_complex": {
      "speech": "Then you can explain why it works, can't you?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Not really.",
          "to": "redstone_begin"
        },
        {
          "text": "Yes. I just wanted a challenge.",
          "to": "puzzles"
        }
      ]
    },
    "redstone_manual": {
      "speech": "Nothing wrong with that. A system isn't better just because it's complicated.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Finally, someone agrees.",
          "to": "planning",
          "effect": "warm"
        },
        {
          "text": "Still, I'd like to learn.",
          "to": "redstone_begin"
        }
      ]
    },
    "puzzles": {
      "speech": "Alright. A simple one: three levers, one door. How would you find which lever matters?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Try one lever at a time.",
          "to": "puzzle_correct"
        },
        {
          "text": "Pull them all and hope.",
          "to": "puzzle_guess"
        },
        {
          "text": "Ask whoever built it.",
          "to": "puzzle_ask"
        }
      ]
    },
    "puzzle_correct": {
      "speech": "Good. Change one variable at a time. Now you know what caused the result.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Was that the point of the puzzle?",
          "to": "puzzle_point"
        },
        {
          "text": "Have you got a harder one?",
          "to": "puzzle_harder"
        }
      ]
    },
    "puzzle_guess": {
      "speech": "And when it opens, you'll have no idea which lever did it.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I see the problem.",
          "to": "puzzle_correct",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "At least it'd be quick.",
          "to": "puzzle_point"
        }
      ]
    },
    "puzzle_ask": {
      "speech": "If they're available, sure. But what if they aren't?",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Then test each lever.",
          "to": "puzzle_correct",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "Then I give up.",
          "to": "puzzle_point"
        }
      ]
    },
    "puzzle_point": {
      "speech": "The point wasn't a clever trick. It was paying attention.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Alright, that makes sense.",
          "to": "puzzle_harder",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "I was expecting more of a riddle.",
          "to": "puzzle_harder"
        }
      ]
    },
    "puzzle_harder": {
      "speech": "Harder problems are usually just simple ones you haven't divided up yet.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "You make it sound manageable.",
          "to": "planning",
          "effect": "warm"
        },
        {
          "text": "I'll keep practising.",
          "to": "redstone"
        }
      ]
    },
    "planning": {
      "speech": "What are we planning? And don't say 'a trip' like that answers everything.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "A safe route out of town.",
          "to": "plan_route"
        },
        {
          "text": "A supply run.",
          "to": "plan_supplies"
        },
        {
          "text": "I just wanted to wander.",
          "to": "plan_wander"
        }
      ]
    },
    "plan_route": {
      "speech": "Distance, food, weather, somewhere to turn back. Those are the basics.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Should I mark a return point?",
          "to": "plan_return",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "That seems like a lot.",
          "to": "plan_wander"
        }
      ]
    },
    "plan_supplies": {
      "speech": "List what you need before you leave. Otherwise you'll buy six things and forget the one that matters.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I can make a list.",
          "to": "plan_return",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "I'm sure I'll remember.",
          "to": "plan_forget"
        }
      ]
    },
    "plan_wander": {
      "speech": "You can wander. Just take enough food to stop it becoming a rescue operation.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Fair enough.",
          "to": "plan_return"
        },
        {
          "text": "You're always this cautious?",
          "to": "plan_caution"
        }
      ]
    },
    "plan_forget": {
      "speech": "Then I look forward to hearing what you forgot.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I'll write it down.",
          "to": "plan_return",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "You're impossible.",
          "to": "plan_caution"
        }
      ]
    },
    "plan_return": {
      "speech": "Good. A decent plan leaves room for things to go wrong.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Thanks. That helped.",
          "to": "town",
          "effect": "warm"
        },
        {
          "text": "What about exploring on instinct?",
          "to": "plan_wander"
        }
      ]
    },
    "plan_caution": {
      "speech": "I'm cautious when it matters. I don't enjoy cleaning up avoidable disasters.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I can see why.",
          "to": "town",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "Sometimes surprises are fun.",
          "to": "town"
        }
      ]
    },
    "town": {
      "speech": "It works. Most days. It could work a bit better.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "What would you change first?",
          "to": "town_fix"
        },
        {
          "text": "Do you ever take a break?",
          "to": "break"
        },
        {
          "text": "You sound pleased for once.",
          "to": "town_dry"
        }
      ]
    },
    "town_fix": {
      "speech": "I'd label storage. People keep putting things wherever there's room.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I would absolutely do that.",
          "to": "town_dry"
        },
        {
          "text": "You'd hate my chest room.",
          "to": "town_mess"
        }
      ]
    },
    "town_mess": {
      "speech": "I don't need to see it. I can already imagine it.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I'll sort it out someday.",
          "to": "town_fix"
        },
        {
          "text": "It's organised chaos.",
          "to": "town_dry"
        }
      ]
    },
    "town_dry": {
      "speech": "Don't make me regret saying something nice.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Wouldn't dream of it.",
          "to": "break",
          "effect": "warm"
        },
        {
          "text": "I should probably let you work.",
          "to": "root"
        }
      ]
    },
    "break": {
      "speech": "Yes. Sometimes. Usually after someone reminds me.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "Consider this your reminder.",
          "to": "break_yes",
          "effect": "trust"
        },
        {
          "text": "You can't keep going forever.",
          "to": "break_yes"
        }
      ]
    },
    "break_yes": {
      "speech": "Fine. Five minutes. You win.",
      "choices": [
        {
          "text": "I'll take the victory.",
          "to": "root",
          "effect": "warm"
        },
        {
          "text": "What do you do when you're not working?",
          "to": "puzzles"
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}